    <briefdescription>
<para>Writes all restart fields in a given restart file to a new restart file <linebreak/>
Example usage: </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>call <ref refid="interfacefms2__io__mod_1_1write__new__restart" kindref="compound">write_new_restart</ref>(fileobj, timestamp=&quot;tstring&quot;, filename=&quot;new_restartfilename&quot;)</para><para>Creates a new restart file, with the provided timestamp and filename, out of the registered restart fields in the given restart fileobj.</para><para><simplesect kind="note"><para>This interface is only intended for use with diskless netcdf files.</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>For individual documentation on the listed routines, please see the appropriate helper module: <ref refid="group__blackboxio" kindref="compound">blackboxio</ref> </para></simplesect>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
